      "path": "app/scanner/runner.py",
      "content": "The suppression cache never observes an explicit resume. After a successful rejection, `resume_input_submission()` changes only the Backend row to `PENDING_INPUT`; it neither clears this journal nor changes the files. If the operator resumes an unchanged, still-invalid bag, every subsequent scan takes this return, leaving the submission pending indefinitely instead of rejecting it again. Tie suppression to the Backend submission generation (and invalidate/reset stability on resume), rather than relying solely on the file snapshot. Add an end-to-end reject → resume without file changes → scan regression test.",
      "existing_code": "        if old.get(\"reject_snapshot\") == snapshot and old.get(\"reject_reported\"):\n            marker[\"reject_snapshot\"] = snapshot\n            marker[\"reject_reason\"] = reason_code\n            marker[\"reject_reported\"] = True\n            stats[\"rejected_suppressed\"] = stats.get(\"rejected_suppressed\", 0) + 1\n            return",
      "start_line": 199,
      "end_line": 204,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "high"
    },
    {
      "path": "app/scanner/runner.py",
      "content": "A previously rejected bag that becomes valid falls through to the existing move/register path without checking whether an explicit resume occurred. For example, adding the missing DB3 and waiting for stability moves the bag out of incoming while its submission is still `INPUT_REJECTED`. With ingest binding enabled, registration then ignores that rejected row and attempts to create a system submission with the same unique path claim, causing registration to fail after the move. Check the authoritative rejection/resume state before allowing a formerly rejected bag to move; corrected files alone must not bypass controlled recovery.",
